{"name":"Tree Pose","hex":"#bdc7bc","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tree","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A perennial woody plant taller and larger than a shrub with a wooden trunk and, at some distance from the ground, having leaves and branches.","Any other plant (such as a large shrub or herb) that is reminiscent of the above in form and size."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To chase (an animal or person) up a tree.","To place in a tree."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tree"},{"term":"pose","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Common cold, head cold; catarrh."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To place in an attitude or fixed position, for the sake of effect.","To ask; to set (a test, quiz, riddle, etc.)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pose"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tree pose","blocks":[{"text":"Tree pose or Vrikshasana is a balancing asana. It is one of the very few standing poses in medieval hatha yoga, and remains popular in modern yoga as exercise. The pose has been called iconic of modern yoga; it is often featured in yoga magazines, and practised in public displays such as for the International Day of Yoga."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/Vriksasana_Yoga-Asana_Nina-Mel.jpg/330px-Vriksasana_Yoga-Asana_Nina-Mel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tree_pose","wikidata":"Q639721"},{"title":"Tree","blocks":[{"text":"In botany, a tree is a perennial plant with an elongated stem, or trunk, usually supporting branches and leaves. In some usages, the definition of a tree may be narrower, e.g., including only woody plants with secondary growth, only plants that are usable for timber, or only plants above a specified height. Wider definitions include taller palms, tree ferns, bananas, and bamboos."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Usamljeni_jasen_-_panoramio_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Usamljeni_jasen_-_panoramio_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tree","wikidata":"Q10884"},{"title":"List of human positions","blocks":[{"text":"Human positions are different physical configurations that the human body can take. There are several synonyms that refer to human positioning, often used interchangeably, but having specific nuances of meaning."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Yoga_%289704376297%29.jpg/330px-Yoga_%289704376297%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_human_positions","wikidata":"Q29034095"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Ganga_Mahabalipuram2.jpg/250px-Ganga_Mahabalipuram2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/34/Ganga_Mahabalipuram2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Ganga_Mahabalipuram2.jpg/250px-Ganga_Mahabalipuram2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGanga_Mahabalipuram2.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/The_Minister_of_State_for_Home_Affairs%2C_Shri_Kiren_Rijiju_performing_Yoga%2C_on_the_occasion_of_the_3rd_International_Day_of_Yoga_%E2%80%93_2017%2C_in_Gangtok%2C_Sikkim_on_June_21%2C_2017_%282%29.jpg/500px-thumbnail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/The_Minister_of_State_for_Home_Affairs%2C_Shri_Kiren_Rijiju_performing_Yoga%2C_on_the_occasion_of_the_3rd_International_Day_of_Yoga_%E2%80%93_2017%2C_in_Gangtok%2C_Sikk